@startuml overview
!include theme.iuml
title Crafty — separate agents, persistent sessions, and FreeCAD evaluation
top to bottom direction

actor "Maker\ncaliper + object" as User
component "Browser\nchat / capture / annotations\nimages / numerical evidence / 3D / downloads" as Web

node "DigitalOcean host · Docker Compose + runtime orchestration" {
  component "Caddy · public HTTPS / WSS\nicrafty.ai" as Edge
  node "Trusted application · Python / uv" #E8F3EC {
    component "API + task coordinator\nmessages / handoffs / evaluation jobs\nassets / result publication / event stream" as API
    storage "Durable metadata + immutable blobs\nsession mappings / tasks / revisions / results" as State
    component "Runtime orchestrator\ncreate / stop / recover containers\nexclusive session ownership + pinned mounts" as Orch
  }

  node "Conversational session A · isolated container" #FFF0E5 {
    component "Supervisor -> ACP adapter -> Codex\nuser dialog / measurements / CAD delegation\nlocal MCP: input requests + fetch / publish files" as Convo
  }
  node "CAD session B · isolated container" #FFF0E5 {
    component "Supervisor -> ACP adapter -> Codex\ncode -> inspect renders / checks -> revise\nlocal MCP: FreeCAD evaluation + file handoff" as Cad
  }
  node "FreeCAD service · bounded execution attempts" #FCE9E7 {
    component "Build native geometry\nrender requested views / compute checks\noptional GLB / STEP export" as FC
    note bottom of FC
      Execution and verification; no reasoning agent.
      Images or numerical results can finish without STEP.
      No network, provider credentials, or Docker socket.
      CPU / memory / process / output / time limits.
    end note
  }

  storage "Session A persistent volumes\nworkspace + private Codex state" as VolA #FFF3CD
  storage "Session B persistent volumes\nworkspace + private Codex state" as VolB #FFF3CD
}

User --> Web
Web --> Edge : application routes + event cursor
Edge --> API
API -right-> State : sole domain state writer
API --> Orch : desired session / job state
Orch --> Convo : start / recover A
Orch --> Cad : start / recover B
Orch --> FC : start / stop attempts
Convo --> VolA : exclusive mount
Cad --> VolB : exclusive mount
Convo -[hidden]right-> Cad
Cad -[hidden]right-> FC

legend bottom
  TRD-5–13: each agent has its own ACP session, container, and persistent mounts.
  Private ACP / MCP data flows and agent handoffs pass through the application; see acp-turn.
  Local file paths are session-local. Shared project assets move through scoped fetch / publication.
  Only the orchestrator has container-control authority. Container removal retains session volumes.
  TRD-21–28: CAD agent owns iteration; FreeCAD provides images, numerical checks, and optional exports.
  Confirmed architecture direction with proposed implementation details; no deployed services implied.
endlegend
@enduml
